    "line_text": "\\unsure{Let us consider} now an arbitrary finite subgroup $G\\subset\\widehat{\\mathcal T}_a^+$. [N.B. If we take \\inserted{only} $G\\subset M_a$, so that the image of $G$ in $\\mathbb{\\Gamma}_a=M_a/\\widehat{\\mathcal T}_a^+$ is a finite subgroup, then if it \\deleted{$\\mathbb{\\Gamma}_a$} is true that $\\mathbb{\\Gamma}_a\\simeq\\unsure{\\mathcal G|\\mathfrak G}$, \\margin{$\\operatorname{Gal}(\\overline{\\mathbb Q}/\\mathbb Q)\\longrightarrow$} this image must be of order $1$ or $2$, and in the second case must \\margin{\\unsure{?}} define a $\\tau\\in\\mathbb{\\Gamma}_a$ corresponding to a well-determined \\uline{\\unsure{prediscretification}} (not oriented) of $\\pi$. This case should be reused again in what follows\\ldots]. \\deleted{If we} \\inserted{Let us suppose, \\unsure{or}} \\unsure{admit}, that $G$ is contained in $\\mathcal T^+$, \\margin{this is probably \\uline{not} automatic (if we \\unsure{do} \\unsure{not|N'} suppose $N_a=\\operatorname{Norm}_{\\widehat{\\widehat{\\mathcal T}}}(\\unsure{\\widehat{\\mathcal T}_a|\\widehat{\\mathcal T}_a^+})$)} for a suitable discretification in the class $a$, and that the outer action of $G$ thus obtained on a discrete $\\pi_0$ of type $(g,\\nu)$ \\unsure{is|are} always \\uline{realizable}. It is therefore also realizable \\unsure{by|for} an action of $G$"
